This directory vendors the SysML v2 ANTLR4 grammar (SysMLv2Parser.g4,
SysMLv2Lexer.g4). The grammar is a third-party artifact, redistributed here
under the MIT License. Two upstream sources are attributed:

1. The ANTLR4 grammar itself, as maintained by the antlr/grammars-v4 project
   (path: sysml-v2).
       Source:  https://github.com/antlr/grammars-v4 (path: sysml-v2)
       License: MIT
       Copyright (c) The respective grammars-v4 contributors.

2. The OMG SysML v2 textual notation that the grammar formalizes, as published
   by the Systems-Modeling/SysML-v2-Release project (tag 2026-01). The grammar
   is derived from the KEBNF in that specification release.
       Source:  https://github.com/Systems-Modeling/SysML-v2-Release (tag 2026-01)
       License: See that repository's LICENSE (the SysML v2 Pilot Implementation
                and release artifacts are distributed under the GNU LGPL v3 /
                accompanying OMG terms; the textual-notation EBNF reproduced
                through the ANTLR grammar is redistributed here under MIT as part
                of the grammars-v4 artifact).

